nt-weight: 433.3;"></span></span></span></button><div class="flex items-center"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="[content-visibility:auto] [contain-intrinsic-size:auto_400px] pb-8 -mb-8 print:[content-visibility:visible]"><div data-test-render-count="1"><div class="group" style="height: auto; opacity: 1; transform: none;"><div class="contents"><div data-is-streaming="false" class="group relative relative pb-3" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><h2 class="sr-only select-none">Claude responded: Yes!</h2><div class="font-claude-response relative leading-[1.65rem] [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:bg-bg-000/50 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-0.5 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-border-400 [&amp;_.ignore-pre-bg&gt;div]:bg-transparent [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8"><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Yes! Location is a big reason it got rejected. Here's how to fix it:</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Best Fix — Apply from College! 🏫</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">The easiest solution is to <strong>go to your college</strong> and apply from there:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Connect to <strong>college WiFi</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Open the application on your <strong>phone or laptop</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">GitHub will automatically detect you're at SAGE University location</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">This is the most reliable method</li>
</ul>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">If you apply from home:</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>On Phone (Mobile Data):</strong></p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Turn off WiFi, use <strong>mobile data only</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to phone Settings → Location → Turn <strong>ON</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Open Chrome → go to education.github.com</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">When browser asks for location → tap <strong>Allow</strong></li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>On Laptop:</strong></p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Windows Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → <strong>Location → ON</strong></li>
