<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">That GitHub sign in popup is just for VS Code — you can close it for now.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Now deploy on Vercel!</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Go to <strong><a class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://vercel.com/">https://vercel.com</a></strong> in your browser</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Click <strong>"Sign Up"</strong> → <strong>"Continue with GitHub"</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Sign in with your <strong>Bhoomi-1401</strong> GitHub account</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Step 4:</strong> Click <strong>"Add New Project"</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Step 5:</strong> You'll see your <strong>Portfolio</strong> repo — click <strong>"Import"</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Step 6:</strong> Just click <strong>"Deploy"</strong> — don't change any settings!</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Step 7:</strong> Wait 2-3 minutes and you'll get a live link! 🚀</p>
