<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 1: Create a new repo on YOUR GitHub</h3>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Go to <strong>github.com</strong> and login as <strong>Bhoomi-1401</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click the <strong>"+"</strong> button → <strong>"New repository"</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Name it: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Portfolio</code></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Keep it <strong>Public</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>"Create repository"</strong></li>
</ol>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 2: Change the remote to YOUR repo</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">In VS Code terminal run:</p>
