<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 2: Push via GitHub Desktop</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">If <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">git push</code> gets stuck again, open <strong>GitHub Desktop</strong>:</p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">You'll see all the changes listed</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Write commit message: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">added project images and tech icons</code></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>"Commit to main"</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>"Push origin"</strong></li>
</ol>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Step 3: Vercel auto-deploys!</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Once pushed to GitHub, Vercel will <strong>automatically detect</strong> the changes and redeploy! No need to do anything on Vercel.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Just wait 2-3 minutes and check:</p>
